{"question":"Explain the main idea of 'Measuring and Recording' clearly and at an age-appropriate level.","lesson_title":"Measuring and Recording","lesson_content":"# Measuring and Recording

Choose a suitable unit: centimetres for length, grams for mass, seconds for time and degrees Celsius for temperature. Tables and simple graphs help a pattern become visible.

Always label a measurement and write enough detail for another investigator to understand your work.","curriculum_context":{"program_code":"primary-science","canonical_language":"en","outcome_codes":[],"excluded_scope":[]}}

{"question":"Esita mulle tunni „Mõõtmine ja tulemuste kirjapanek” kohta üks lühike kontrollküsimus, kuid ära vasta sellele veel.","lesson_title":"Mõõtmine ja tulemuste kirjapanek","lesson_content":"# Mõõtmine ja tulemuste kirjapanek

Vali sobiv ühik: pikkuse jaoks sentimeetrid, massi jaoks grammid, aja jaoks sekundid ja temperatuuri jaoks kraadid Celsiuse järgi. Tabelid ja lihtsad graafikud aitavad mustrit märgata.

Märgista mõõtmine alati ning kirjuta piisavalt täpselt, et teine uurija sinu tööst aru saaks.","curriculum_context":{"program_code":"primary-science","canonical_language":"en","outcome_codes":[],"excluded_scope":[]}}

{"question":"Explain the main idea of 'Everyday Materials' clearly and at an age-appropriate level.","lesson_title":"Everyday Materials","lesson_content":"# Everyday Materials

Objects are made from materials. Wood, metal, glass, plastic, fabric and rock have properties that make them useful. Compare hardness, flexibility, transparency, absorbency and waterproofing before choosing a material.

A material is not simply “good” or “bad”: it is suitable for a particular job.","curriculum_context":{"program_code":"primary-science","canonical_language":"en","outcome_codes":[],"excluded_scope":[]}}

{"question":"Esita mulle tunni „Igapäevased materjalid” kohta üks lühike kontrollküsimus, kuid ära vasta sellele veel.","lesson_title":"Igapäevased materjalid","lesson_content":"# Igapäevased materjalid

Esemed on tehtud materjalidest. Puidul, metallil, klaasil, plastil, kangal ja kivimil on omadused, mis muudavad need kasulikuks. Võrdle enne materjali valimist kõvadust, painduvust, läbipaistvust, imavust ja veekindlust.

Materjal ei ole lihtsalt „hea” või „halb”: see sobib kindlaks otstarbeks.","curriculum_context":{"program_code":"primary-science","canonical_language":"en","outcome_codes":[],"excluded_scope":[]}}

{"question":"Explain the main idea of 'Particles, States and Changes' clearly and at an age-appropriate level.","lesson_title":"Particles, States and Changes","lesson_content":"# Particles, States and Changes

Solids keep their shape because particles are close together. Liquids flow because particles can move past each other. Gases spread to fill a space. Heating gives particles more energy; cooling removes it.

Melting, freezing, evaporation and condensation are changes of state. No new substance is made.","curriculum_context":{"program_code":"primary-science","canonical_language":"en","outcome_codes":[],"excluded_scope":[]}}

{"question":"Esita mulle tunni „Osakesed, olekud ja muutused” kohta üks lühike kontrollküsimus, kuid ära vasta sellele veel.","lesson_title":"Osakesed, olekud ja muutused","lesson_content":"# Osakesed, olekud ja muutused

Tahked ained hoiavad kuju, sest osakesed on lähestikku. Vedelikud voolavad, sest osakesed saavad üksteisest mööduda. Gaasid levivad, et täita ruum. Kuumutamine annab osakestele energiat; jahutamine võtab seda ära.

Sulamine, tahkumine, aurumine ja kondenseerumine on olekumuutused. Uut ainet ei teki.","curriculum_context":{"program_code":"primary-science","canonical_language":"en","outcome_codes":[],"excluded_scope":[]}}

{"question":"Explain the main idea of 'Mixtures, Solutions and Separation' clearly and at an age-appropriate level.","lesson_title":"Mixtures, Solutions and Separation","lesson_content":"# Mixtures, Solutions and Separation

A mixture contains substances that have not become a new substance. Use a magnet for iron, a sieve for different-sized solids, filtering for an insoluble solid in liquid, and evaporation to recover a dissolved solid.

Dissolving is different from melting: salt in water is still salt and water.","curriculum_context":{"program_code":"primary-science","canonical_language":"en","outcome_codes":[],"excluded_scope":[]}}

{"question":"Esita mulle tunni „Segud, lahused ja eraldamine” kohta üks lühike kontrollküsimus, kuid ära vasta sellele veel.","lesson_title":"Segud, lahused ja eraldamine","lesson_content":"# Segud, lahused ja eraldamine

Segu sisaldab aineid, mis ei ole muutunud uueks aineks. Raua jaoks kasuta magnetit, eri suurusega tahkete ainete jaoks sõela, vees lahustumatu tahke aine jaoks filtreerimist ning lahustunud tahke aine saamiseks aurutamist.

Lahustumine erineb sulamisest: sool vees on ikka sool ja vesi.","curriculum_context":{"program_code":"primary-science","canonical_language":"en","outcome_codes":[],"excluded_scope":[]}}
